Debian 13 update (2026-10-01)
----------------------------
See QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13 for the native amd64/arm64 package qualification.
Ubuntu-only scope statements below describe the initial packaging checkpoint.

Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the Cairo module
===========================================

qore-cairo-module ships native Cairo, the CairoDataProvider source/AOT module,
qsvg and its manual, compiler metadata, provider resources and locale catalogs.
The doc package contains both API references and example tests. Debhelper
creates matching native and AOT debug symbols.

Use an isolated native environment with packaged Qore and libqore-dev, then
install debian/control's Build-Depends. Qualification targets Ubuntu 26.04
amd64 with Qore 3.0. Other targets need matching SDKs and native tests. Cross
builds fail explicitly because Qore tools execute during compilation. System
Cairo/librsvg are used; no bundled libraries or build-time downloads are needed.
SVG input and PDF output are required and verified in build/installed tests.
DejaVu fonts provide a default font for the text APIs and CLI without a desktop.

The minimum Qore runtime and libqore SONAME versions come from the installed
SDK; dh_shlibdeps supplies the other library dependencies. The runtime package
is not Multi-Arch: same. AOT is enabled, source-tree qmod symlinks are disabled,
and noopt selects optimization level zero. QCC_JOBS=1 fixes partitioning across
CPU counts/jobserver loads while independent targets still compile in parallel.
Qore tools use the build and packaged standard library only. Prefix maps cover
native/AOT output; timezone and locale are fixed.

The stripping wrapper copied from Qore preserves appended AOT metadata and
its real-ELF tests run during the build. dwz excludes unsupported LLVM DWARF.
All provider catalogs and the ownership manifest are packaged; the complete
standard-locale check runs against the built provider via qore-misc-tools.

Source preparation and qualification
------------------------------------

Use a fresh version for each changed upload. This snapshot precedes 1.0.0.
From a clean committed checkout:

    version=1.0.0~git20260928.1
    mkdir -p ../cairo-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-cairo-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' | xz > \
        "../cairo-package-work/qore-cairo-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../cairo-package-work/qore-cairo-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../cairo-package-work
    cp -a debian "../cairo-package-work/qore-cairo-module-$version/"
    cd "../cairo-package-work/qore-cairo-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc into a fresh directory and run dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc
unprivileged offline. -B builds runtime/debug only; -A builds documentation.
nodoc in DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS suppresses HTML, and the nodoc profile also omits
the doc package. Full qualification runs tests; repeated/profile builds may
use nocheck.

Run both upstream suites, complete catalogs, AOT helper tests and the CLI
checks. Installed tests copy only test scripts to a temporary directory and
preload the installed AOT provider. CLI checks cover SVG creation, PNG/PDF
conversion, text rendering, paths with spaces and explicit in-place resizing. A
fresh qcc executable tests named arguments, PNG round trip, optional feature
availability and provider factory discovery. No external service is needed.

Check Lintian, hardening/debug symbols, AOT trailers, source/resource/catalog
parity, runtime-only installation without SDK, docs/debug coinstallation,
dpkg -V, purge/reinstall and byte reproducibility across paths/job counts.
Retain hashes, dependency inventories and logs. Testing-PPA publication is
separate from approval for a final general release.
